# Offline oracle note — dfpt-spin-incommensurate

## Intent

Twin for **collinear-spin** DFPT phonons at **incommensurate** fractional q
on diamond Si (PW LSDA, NC-UPF). Atomiverse path:
`cpu::pw::DfptPhonon` with `spin_polarized=true`, multiplicity=1,
`q_frac = {0.3, 0.0, 0.0}` → direct `internal::dfpt_q_force_constants`
spin channel (`dfpt_q_spin_impl`).

## Preferred CP2K twin (when binary available)

- Structure: 2-atom FCC Si, a = 5.43 Å
- Method: Quickstep / VIBRATIONAL_ANALYSIS or DFPT at non-Γ q with LSD/UKS
- Functional: LDA / PADE-like; comparable NC or GTH setup
- Spin: collinear, M = 0
- Record: ω(q) [cm⁻¹] (6 branches), wall time, CP2K version

## This host

CP2K binary **not available**. Pins are literature-biased windows aligned
with the restricted incommensurate twin (`dfpt-incommensurate-si`) plus
measured ATV collinear-spin spectrum under the regression settings (see
`regressions/response/dfpt-spin-incommensurate/REFERENCE.md`).
`perf_exempt=true` until a fair CP2K DFPT wall is recorded.

## Cite

Baroni et al., Rev. Mod. Phys. 73, 515 (2001);
Giannozzi et al., Phys. Rev. B 43, 7231 (1991).
